** Key Benefits of Cloud Computing **
[Script]
[Benefits icons appear on screen]

The benefits of cloud computing are numerous and that's why it's become so popular in recent years. In this section, we'll highlight some of the key advantages:

- Cost Efficiency: You pay only for what you use, reducing costs compared to maintaining your own infrastructure.
  Instead of buying and managing servers, hiring staff to maintain them, and paying for power 24/7, you can simply start small with a few virtual machines and grow as needed.
  Cloud computing removes the upfront investment and ensures you’re never paying for idle resources.

- Scalability: Cloud computing lets you scale your resources up or down instantly based on demand, ensuring optimal performance without over-provisioning.
  For instance, if your app gains new users, you can expand capacity automatically—no downtime, no manual effort, and no wasted resources when demand drops.

- Global scale: Deploy your applications closer to your users, anywhere in the world.
  With over 300 data centers across more than 60 Azure regions, you can host your apps near your audience to reduce latency and improve reliability.
  This global reach helps deliver a consistent, high-quality experience to users everywhere.

- Security: Cloud providers like Microsoft Azure invest heavily in cybersecurity to protect your data and applications.
  Microsoft spends billions annually and employs thousands of security experts who monitor systems, perform audits, and enforce strict compliance standards—so your workloads stay secure by default.

- Performance: You always run on the latest, most powerful hardware—without needing to upgrade anything yourself.
  Azure continuously refreshes its infrastructure to give you high-performance computing, fast networking, and optimized storage, so your apps always run efficiently.

- Reliability: Cloud platforms provide built-in high availability, redundancy, and disaster recovery.
  Even if hardware fails, your applications stay online thanks to Azure’s backup and recovery options.
  That means better uptime, safer data, and uninterrupted user experiences.

